<main class="wide app-ledger">

::: section #ledger

:theme
:store expenses = [
  {"id":1,"date":"2026-06-22","merchant":"Aurora Studio","category":"Software","amount":149},
  {"id":2,"date":"2026-06-20","merchant":"Briza Coffee","category":"Meals","amount":18.4},
  {"id":3,"date":"2026-06-19","merchant":"Cobalt Cloud","category":"Hosting","amount":312.5},
  {"id":4,"date":"2026-06-18","merchant":"Dune Print Co","category":"Office","amount":64},
  {"id":5,"date":"2026-06-16","merchant":"Aurora Studio","category":"Software","amount":29},
  {"id":6,"date":"2026-06-15","merchant":"Ember Transit","category":"Travel","amount":212.75},
  {"id":7,"date":"2026-06-13","merchant":"Briza Coffee","category":"Meals","amount":11.2},
  {"id":8,"date":"2026-06-11","merchant":"Cobalt Cloud","category":"Hosting","amount":312.5}
]
:state q = ""
:state sortKey = "amount"
:state sortDir = "desc"
:state secs = 0
:every 1s -> secs++

:computed total = sum(expenses, amount)
:computed average = avg(expenses, amount)
:computed largest = max(expenses, amount)

::: ledger-head
::: ledger-mark
::: eyebrow .ledger-eyebrow
A real data table
:::

# *Ledger*

::: ledger-tagline
Clickable-header sorting, a live filter, and running totals — a spreadsheet-grade table written as one Markdown file. The numbers below are `{ … | money }`; the dates are `{ … | date }`; the totals are `sum()` / `avg()` / `max()`.
:::
:::

::: theme-switch
Theme
:button "Auto" -> theme = "auto"
:button "Light" -> theme = "light"
:button "Dark" -> theme = "dark"
:::
:::

::: stat-grid
::: card .stat
::: stat-label
Total spend
:::
::: stat-num
{ total | money }
:::
:::
::: card .stat
::: stat-label
Average
:::
::: stat-num
{ average | money }
:::
:::
::: card .stat
::: stat-label
Largest
:::
::: stat-num
{ largest | money }
:::
:::
::: card .stat
::: stat-label
Entries
:::
::: stat-num
{ expenses | count }
:::
:::
:::

::: ledger-controls
:bind q placeholder="Filter by merchant…"
::: synced
↻ live · { secs | pluralize:"second" } on this page
:::
:::

::: card .ledger-table

::: thead
::: th .active when sortKey == "date"
:button "Date" -> sortKey = "date" ; sortDir = "asc"
:::
::: th .active when sortKey == "merchant"
:button "Merchant" -> sortKey = "merchant" ; sortDir = "asc"
:::
::: th .active when sortKey == "category"
:button "Category" -> sortKey = "category" ; sortDir = "asc"
:::
::: th .num .active when sortKey == "amount"
:button "Amount" -> sortKey = "amount" ; sortDir = "desc"
:::
::: th .dir
:button "▲" -> sortDir = "asc"
:button "▼" -> sortDir = "desc"
:::
:::

@loop expenses into e where e.merchant contains q sort by { sortKey } { sortDir }
::: trow
::: td .muted
{ e.date | date:"medium" }
:::
::: td .strong
{ e.merchant }
:::
::: td
::: pill
{ e.category }
:::
:::
::: td .num
{ e.amount | money }
:::
::: td .dir
:button "✕" -> expenses remove e
:::
:::
@empty
::: trow .blank
No expenses match "**{ q }**".
:::
@endloop

:::

::: ledger-foot
{ expenses | count } entries · totalling **{ total | money }** · sorted by **{ sortKey }** ({ sortDir })
:::

<details class="source-reveal">
<summary>View source — it's Markdown</summary>

```wd
:store expenses = [ … ]
:state sortKey = "amount"
:state sortDir = "desc"
:state q = ""

:computed total = sum(expenses, amount)

# clickable headers set the sort column + direction
:button "Amount" -> sortKey = "amount" ; sortDir = "desc"
:button "▲" -> sortDir = "asc"

:bind q placeholder="Filter by merchant…"

@loop expenses into e where e.merchant contains q sort by { sortKey } { sortDir }
| { e.date | date:"medium" } | { e.merchant } | { e.amount | money } |
:button "✕" -> expenses remove e
@endloop

Total: { total | money }
```

</details>

